      en: "Mazenod is a village in the Maseru District of Lesotho, located 20 kilometers southeast of Maseru. It is centered around a Catholic mission established by the Oblate Fathers, who run a school and a health clinic. Agriculture (maize, beans) and commuting to Maseru for employment are the main economic activities. The village has a population of a few thousand and serves as a rural suburb of the capital.",
